{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"N98\",\"lines\":\"r--r--n-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N98.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَّرْضَىٰٓ\",\"target_ar\":\"قُمْتُمْ\",\"after\":\"The rise toward prayer is heard against effort that slackens and falls short. The command gathers the ill into renewed movement rather than treating weakness as refusal.\",\"reason\":\"مَّرْضَىٰ carries the rare sense of weakened striving, while قُمْتُمْ is resolute rising to an undertaking. Failing motion and determined rising oppose one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N98.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَّرْضَىٰٓ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The illness clause names diminished effort, yet the substitute begins with deliberate aim. Purposeful direction answers an incapacity to carry on the ordinary course.\",\"reason\":\"مَّرْضَىٰ can mean falling short in effort; فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟ means intentionally aiming toward something. The near-failure and purposeful aiming pull in opposite directions.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N98.7\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَّرْضَىٰٓ\",\"target_ar\":\"حَرَجٍ\",\"after\":\"Weak effort and constriction both suggest action becoming difficult.\",\"reason\":\"The rare مرض sense is effort left slack or incomplete, while حَرَجٍ is tightness and constraint; both images limit movement.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N99\",\"lines\":\"-rn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N99.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَّرْضَىٰٓ\",\"target_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"after\":\"The journey condition can be heard as daylight clearing a veil beside illness as light going dim. The alternatives place exposure and obscurity in one field.\",\"reason\":\"مَّرْضَىٰ has a rare sense of dim, unbright light; سَفَرٍ can mean the lifting of a covering and the brightening of dawn. Waning light and unveiled brightness oppose each other.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N99.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَّرْضَىٰٓ\",\"target_ar\":\"نِعْمَتَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"The dimming image can make a good condition sound like light that has waned.\",\"reason\":\"The rare مرض sense is diminished brightness, while نِعْمَتَهُۥ is well-being and favor; the two meet as light and the loss of well-being.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N100\",\"lines\":\"--r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N100.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَّرْضَىٰٓ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The sick condition is imagined as effort approaching its aim but stopping short. Tayammum directs the person toward a chosen clean surface, giving the concession a reachable aim.\",\"reason\":\"The rare مرض sense is nearly attaining a goal without reaching it; فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟ is deliberate aiming toward an object. The verse sets frustrated approach beside purposeful direction.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N101\",\"lines\":\"rrrrr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N101.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"قُمْتُمْ\",\"after\":\"The rising toward prayer can carry the image of daybreak brightening. The believers rise as the light opens the day.\",\"reason\":\"سَفَرٍ has the rare sense of dawn brightening and darkness being uncovered; قُمْتُمْ is rising toward an undertaking. Their senses make a picture of rising with the day.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N101.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The face washed for prayer is heard as a face made bright. The washing scene gains an image of light appearing on its surface.\",\"reason\":\"سَفَرٍ can mean a luminous, shining face; وُجُوهَكُمْ names the face and its forward-facing side. The rare sense of brightness falls directly on the face in the command.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N101.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The brightening of day accompanies the feet that walk. The verse’s journey condition and its walking feet meet in daylight travel.\",\"reason\":\"سَفَرٍ can mean the brightening of dawn or day, while وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ carries the sense of walking on feet. Daylight and walking complement one another as the conditions for travel.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N101.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"صَعِيدًا\",\"after\":\"The selected earth is pictured as a surface brought into the light. The rare sense makes the clean ground visible as dawn uncovers it.\",\"reason\":\"سَفَرٍ can mean brightness that clears darkness; صَعِيدًا is the face of the earth. The brightening and the ground’s exposed surface make one image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N101.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِوُجُوهِكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The face retained in tayammum is heard in the light of the brightening sense. Even the reduced rite presents the face as a surface made clear.\",\"reason\":\"سَفَرٍ carries the rare image of a luminous, shining face; بِوُجُوهِكُمْ names the faces touched with earth. Their shared picture is a face made bright and brought forward.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N102\",\"lines\":\"rnnrrn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N102.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The traveler leaves a place and takes a direction. The face as a way or destination complements the journey’s movement away from home.\",\"reason\":\"سَفَرٍ in its rare sense is going out on a journey and covering distance; وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean direction or destination. A traveler and the way faced meet as complements.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N102.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْمَرَافِقِ\",\"after\":\"Traveling together and acting with ease can meet in the image of companions helping one another on the way.\",\"reason\":\"سَفَرٍ can mean travelers setting out, while ٱلْمَرَافِقِ carries ease and gentle action; their relation is the general one of journeying with helpful company.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N102.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Crossing terrain and passing a hand over a surface share a faint image of movement across something.\",\"reason\":\"The rare travel sense of سَفَرٍ includes covering distance across the earth; وَٱمْسَحُوا۟ is passing a hand over something. They meet in traversing a surface, though at different scales.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N102.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The journey condition is heard through the feet that carry a traveler. Walking is one bodily means of covering the distance named by travel.\",\"reason\":\"سَفَرٍ can mean journeying and covering distance; وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ carries the plain sense of walking on feet. Walking forms one part of traveling.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N102.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"مَّرْضَىٰٓ\",\"after\":\"The verse names illness and travel as conditions that call for accommodation. The rare travel sense and the illness sense both picture departure from a usual place: one from home, the other from bodily health.\",\"reason\":\"سَفَرٍ can mean leaving one’s place on a journey; مَّرْضَىٰ is departure from health and balance. Their shared image is being away from a normal home or state.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N102.6\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَفَرٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Journeying across land and wiping with earth share an image of passing over a surface.\",\"reason\":\"The rare travel sense of سَفَرٍ is covering distance; فَٱمْسَحُوا۟ is passing a hand over something. Their connection is a general image of crossing a surface.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N103\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N104\",\"lines\":\"r-n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N104.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"أَحَدٌ\",\"after\":\"The clause singles out one person who comes, while the rare sense evokes prevailing through repeated arrivals. The isolated arrival stands out against a crowding influx.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ can carry the rare sense of overcoming through many arrivals; أَحَدٌ is one individual. A multitude of arrivals and the single person oppose one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N104.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"نِعْمَتَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"The rare abundance of arriving can faintly echo favor arriving in abundance.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of جَآءَ is prevailing through plentiful coming; نِعْمَتَهُۥ is favor and well-being. They meet in the general image of good arriving.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N105\",\"lines\":\"r-rn-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N105.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The water gathered in a hollow becomes an available cleansing medium. The image joins collected water to the washing commanded in the verse.\",\"reason\":\"The rare جَآءَ sense is water collecting in a depression or around a fortress; فَٱغْسِلُوا۟ means washing away dirt with water. A pool of water complements the act that uses it.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N105.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ\",\"after\":\"The hollow is pictured as a place where water gathers. The word for the low place and the rare water-pool image form one scene.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ can evoke a gathering of water in a hollow; ٱلْغَآئِطِ in its plain sense is a low, sunken place. The two senses make the picture of a pool in a depression.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N105.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"مَآءً\",\"after\":\"A rare sense of a gathered water pool meets the plain word for water.\",\"reason\":\"The rare جَآءَ image is a collection of water; مَآءً names water itself, so the connection is direct but generic.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N106\",\"lines\":\"-rn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N106.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"كُنتُمْ\",\"after\":\"The conditional state is heard as a condition that has come into presence. The concession applies to an actually present circumstance, not an abstraction.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ has the rare sense of bringing something into presence; كُنتُمْ signals being and presence in time. Both senses meet in presence.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N106.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"لِيَجْعَلَ\",\"after\":\"Bringing something into presence and making it share a broad sense of causing something to be.\",\"reason\":\"The rare جَآءَ sense is bringing a thing into presence; لِيَجْعَلَ is making or producing something. Their connection is real but general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N107\",\"lines\":\"n-nrrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N107.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of compulsion adds a faint image of hands whose agency is under pressure.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ can mean forcing or compelling; وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ can mean hands as power and agency. The senses meet in the image of compelled agency.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N107.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"after\":\"The hands used in tayammum carry a faint image of action performed under necessity.\",\"reason\":\"The rare جَآءَ sense is compulsion or necessity, while وَأَيْدِيكُم can mean hands as agency and capacity. The connection is the general image of necessity bearing on action.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N107.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"after\":\"The verse denies a coercive purpose and then states what God does will: purification and completion of favor. The contrast makes divine will sound purposeful without being compulsion.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ has the rare sense of forcing or compelling, while يُرِيدُ means willing and intending. Compulsion and will stand in opposition in the statement of divine purpose.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N107.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"لِيَجْعَلَ\",\"after\":\"The denied making of hardship is heard as the imposition of a necessity. The verse says that burden is not something God wills to force upon the believers.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ can mean compelling someone into necessity; لِيَجْعَلَ means making or bringing about. Compulsion is one way a hardship could be imposed.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N107.6\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"حَرَجٍ\",\"after\":\"The verse’s denied hardship takes on the force of a denied compulsion. Constraint and distress name the same pressure from two angles.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ can mean compelling or placing someone under necessity; حَرَجٍ is constriction and hardship. The rare compulsion sense and the plain hardship sense meet directly.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N108\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N109\",\"lines\":\"-rr-nn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N109.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"كُنتُمْ\",\"after\":\"The arrival sense and the condition of being present reinforce one another. The verse’s state condition sounds like an event that has come to be.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ means coming or arriving, while كُنتُمْ signals presence and occurrence in time. The two senses meet in being present.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N109.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"كُنتُم\",\"after\":\"The new concession begins from a condition that has come about. Arrival and being present give the condition a concrete sense.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ carries the sense of coming; كُنتُم marks being present in a state. The senses meet in a condition that has come to be.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N109.5\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"تَجِدُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Coming upon something and finding it share a broad sense of encounter.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ is arrival or coming, while تَجِدُوا۟ is finding or encountering. Their connection is close but general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N109.6\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"نِعْمَتَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"The arriving sense can faintly picture favor as something that comes to its recipients.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ means coming or arrival; نِعْمَتَهُۥ means favor and well-being. They meet in the general image of favor arriving.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N110\",\"lines\":\"rrn-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N110.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Water gathered in a pool can serve the washing that the verse commands. The rare image makes the cleansing medium visible as collected water.\",\"reason\":\"The rare جَآءَ sense is a pool or gathering of water; فَٱغْسِلُوا۟ is washing with water to remove dirt. A collected pool complements the act of washing.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N110.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ\",\"after\":\"The rare water-pool image settles into the low hollow named by ٱلْغَآئِطِ. Together they picture water collected in a depression.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ can mean a gathered pool of water; ٱلْغَآئِطِ plainly means a low or sunken place. The senses make one landscape image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N110.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"target_ar\":\"مَآءً\",\"after\":\"The pooled-water sense meets the plain mention of water.\",\"reason\":\"The rare جَآءَ image is gathered water, and مَآءً names water. This is a direct but generic relation.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N111\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N112\",\"lines\":\"----r-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N112.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ءَامَنُوٓا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱللَّهُ\",\"after\":\"The believers’ affirmation is directed toward the One they worship. Faith and its divine object complete one another in the address.\",\"reason\":\"ءَامَنُوٓا۟ carries the rare sense of affirming and trusting as true; ٱللَّهُ is the worshipped One. Affirmation and the One affirmed form a complementary pair.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N112.7\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ءَامَنُوٓا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"تَشْكُرُونَ\",\"after\":\"Faith and gratitude are heard as two forms of acknowledgment. The close of the verse links trusting the divine promise with recognizing favor and responding to it.\",\"reason\":\"ءَامَنُوٓا۟ can mean affirming something as true; تَشْكُرُونَ means recognizing a favor and praising its giver. Both are acts of acknowledgment, though gratitude adds a response.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N113\",\"lines\":\"-rn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N113.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ءَامَنُوٓا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱللَّهُ\",\"after\":\"The rare supplicatory sense is heard as an address directed to God. The prayer phrase and its divine addressee belong together.\",\"reason\":\"ءَامَنُوٓا۟ can carry the rare sense of saying آمين, asking for a response; ٱللَّهُ is the One worshipped. A supplication complements its divine addressee.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N113.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ءَامَنُوٓا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"نِعْمَتَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"A request for an answer can faintly meet the favor that the verse says God completes.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ءَامَنُوٓا۟ is the prayer response آمين, asking that something be so; نِعْمَتَهُۥ is favor. A request and its hoped-for good are related, though generally.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N114\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N115\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N116\",\"lines\":\"------\"}\n{\"id\":\"N117\",\"lines\":\"-n-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N117.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَحَدٌ\",\"target_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"after\":\"The one-by-one sense echoes the singular coming in the clause.\",\"reason\":\"أَحَدٌ can mean coming separately, one by one; جَآءَ means came. Their connection is direct but already close to the clause’s plain wording.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N118\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N119\",\"lines\":\"nrn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N119.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Sinking into water is one possible form of contact within washing.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلْغَآئِطِ is entering or disappearing into something; فَٱغْسِلُوا۟ is washing with water. Immersion can be part of washing, though the verse does not require it.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N119.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The feet that walk can be pictured sinking into the ground beneath them. The rare sense turns the walking feet into an image of penetration into earth.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ can mean sinking or disappearing into something, including sand that swallows footprints; وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ carries walking on feet. Together they picture feet sinking into the ground as one walks.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N119.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ\",\"target_ar\":\"مَآءً\",\"after\":\"The sense of disappearing into a medium meets the verse’s mention of water.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلْغَآئِطِ includes sinking into water; مَآءً names water itself. The relation is immersion and its medium.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N120\",\"lines\":\"r--r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N120.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The bodily event and the washing command meet as impurity and its cleansing response. The later concession preserves that response when water is absent.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ has the rare euphemistic sense of defecation or excrement; فَٱغْسِلُوا۟ means washing away dirt. The bodily event complements the purification action.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N120.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ\",\"target_ar\":\"طَيِّبًا\",\"after\":\"The bodily waste is set against the wholesome, clean earth selected for the substitute rite. The verse moves from impurity toward a clean medium.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ can euphemistically mean excrement; طَيِّبًا means wholesome and clean, opposite to what is filthy. The two senses make a direct contrast.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N121\",\"lines\":\"---r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N121.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ\",\"target_ar\":\"صَعِيدًا\",\"after\":\"The body bends down toward the earth’s surface for tayammum. The rare downward motion and the selected ground make a single physical image.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ can mean lowering by bending; صَعِيدًا is the surface of the earth. The act of lowering toward the ground joins the two senses.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N122\",\"lines\":\"rnnn-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N122.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"target_ar\":\"تَجِدُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Seeking and finding form an effort and its result, here explicitly denied. The verse’s failure to find water follows the search-like sense carried by touch.\",\"reason\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ can mean seeking something by hand, while تَجِدُوا۟ means finding or encountering it. The search and its hoped-for finding complement one another, even as the verse negates the result.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N122.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Searching for something and intentionally aiming toward it share purposeful seeking.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of لَٰمَسْتُمُ is seeking or searching repeatedly; فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟ is intentionally aiming toward a thing. The relation is real but general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N122.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"target_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of seeking a need comes close to the will expressed by يُرِيدُ.\",\"reason\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ can mean wanting or seeking to obtain something; يُرِيدُ means willing or desiring. The senses are near equivalents.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N122.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"target_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"after\":\"The same search-like sense can echo the second statement of divine intent, now directed to purification.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of لَٰمَسْتُمُ is seeking a need; this يُرِيدُ states an intended aim. Seeking and intending overlap, though broadly.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N123\",\"lines\":\"n--rr--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N123.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Intercourse and wiping both involve bodily contact, though the link is broad.\",\"reason\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ can euphemistically mean intercourse; وَٱمْسَحُوا۟ is passing a hand over something. Contact is part of intercourse and is also the physical motion of wiping.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N123.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلنِّسَآءَ\",\"after\":\"The rare euphemism makes the women named in the clause participants in an intimate act. This sharpens the contact condition before the verse gives its purification alternative.\",\"reason\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ can euphemistically mean sexual intercourse; ٱلنِّسَآءَ names women as the categorical object. The women and the intimate act complete one another in the clause.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N123.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The intimate act becomes a condition followed by the wiping rite when water is unavailable. The verse links bodily contact to a reduced purification action.\",\"reason\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ can euphemistically mean intercourse; فَٱمْسَحُوا۟ commands wiping with the selected earth. The intimate act is a trigger, and wiping is the stated substitute response.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N124\",\"lines\":\"nnn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N124.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"target_ar\":\"مَّرْضَىٰٓ\",\"after\":\"A nearby need and illness both suggest a condition that calls for accommodation.\",\"reason\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ can carry the rare sense of a near need; مَّرْضَىٰ is illness and loss of strength. Illness can create need, though the relation is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N124.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"target_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"after\":\"Need and desire meet in the wish to obtain something.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of لَٰمَسْتُمُ is a need or demand; يُرِيدُ means willing or desiring. They overlap in wanting, but only broadly.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N124.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"target_ar\":\"حَرَجٍ\",\"after\":\"A nearby need can arise under the pressure of constriction.\",\"reason\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ can mean a near or pressing need; حَرَجٍ is tightness and hardship. The need and the condition that prompts it are complementary.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N125\",\"lines\":\"-rnn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N125.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَجِدُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْكَعْبَيْنِ\",\"after\":\"The ankle boundary is marked by a raised bone, and the rare sense of greatness carries elevation. The body’s protruding landmark gives a concrete image to the elevated sense.\",\"reason\":\"تَجِدُوا۟ has the rare sense of greatness and elevation; ٱلْكَعْبَيْنِ are protruding, raised ankle bones. Both senses meet in elevation and prominence.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N125.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَجِدُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"طَيِّبًا\",\"after\":\"Greatness and goodness meet in the general idea of value.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of تَجِدُوا۟ is greatness or high worth; طَيِّبًا means good or wholesome. The connection is one of value, but it is broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N125.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَجِدُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"نِعْمَتَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"The completion of favor can be heard with an image of abundance and grandeur.\",\"reason\":\"تَجِدُوا۟ can carry a rare sense of greatness or overflowing bounty; نِعْمَتَهُۥ is favor and well-being. Their connection is the general image of a great favor.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N126\",\"lines\":\"-nr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N126.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَجِدُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْكَعْبَيْنِ\",\"after\":\"Good fortune and a protruding bone share a faint image of being raised or prominent.\",\"reason\":\"تَجِدُوا۟ can mean fortune or elevated worldly standing; ٱلْكَعْبَيْنِ are raised ankle bones. The link is a general image of elevation.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N126.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَجِدُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"نِعْمَتَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of worldly fortune meets the favor God completes for the believers. The verse’s favor is heard as well-being and a good portion received.\",\"reason\":\"تَجِدُوا۟ can mean good fortune, wealth, or a person’s share in prosperity; نِعْمَتَهُۥ means favor and well-being. Both name forms of good received.\"}"}}
